Package: deseq2reports
Title: Modular DESeq2 Pipeline with Automated HTML Reports
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person(given = "Miu Shing", family = "Hung", email = "matthewhungms@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0004-0412-4374"))
Description: A self-contained, modular pipeline for RNA-seq differential expression
    analysis built on DESeq2. Provides a single one-command entry point
    (run_deseq2_pipeline()) that chains quality control, sample distance/PCA,
    differential expression across all pairwise and one-vs-rest group comparisons,
    gene set enrichment analysis (GSEA) against MSigDB collections, and a rendered
    HTML report -- as well as standalone modular functions for each stage so that
    individual steps can be run, inspected, or substituted independently. All
    behaviour that analysts commonly need to change per-analysis (count filtering
    thresholds, batch correction method, LFC shrinkage estimator, significance
    thresholds, ranking metric, MSigDB collections, colour palettes) is exposed
    as explicit function arguments with validated defaults.
